        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The point $O$ shown in the diagram.\n\nExtend lines through corresponding vertices to their intersection.",
          "worked": "Draw lines through corresponding vertices of the two squares. Their intersection is the centre $O$, halfway across and halfway down the grid cell shown.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p12-q7-b-solution",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 12, question 7; teacher page 75\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.8cm,y=-0.8cm]\n\\definecolor{houseGrid}{HTML}{CCCCCC}\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (0,0) rectangle (8,8);\n\\foreach \\v in {0,...,8}{\\draw[houseGrid,line width=0.25pt] (\\v,0)--(\\v,8);}\n\\foreach \\v in {0,...,8}{\\draw[houseGrid,line width=0.25pt] (0,\\v)--(8,\\v);}\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (1,1) rectangle (7,7);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (2,4) rectangle (4,6);\n\\draw[black,dashed,line width=0.4pt] (2.5,5.5)--(1,1);\n\\draw[black,dashed,line width=0.4pt] (2.5,5.5)--(7,1);\n\\draw[black,dashed,line width=0.4pt] (2.5,5.5)--(7,7);\n\\draw[black,dashed,line width=0.4pt] (2.5,5.5)--(1,7);\n\\fill[black] (2.5,5.5) circle (1.2pt);\n\\node[below right,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont] at (2.5,5.5) {$O$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 70,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
              "axes": null,
              "spec": {
                "sourcePage": 12,
                "sourceRegion": "Question 7 shared grid",
                "description": "Complete supplied figure with dashed lines through corresponding vertices and a marked centre.",
                "mathematics": "The centre is (2.5,5.5) in the top-left, downward-positive coordinate frame. Each larger vertex lies three times as far from O as its corresponding smaller vertex.",
                "answerVisibility": "Construction lines and O appear only in answers."
              },
              "derived": false,
              "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
            }
          ]
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
